  fhir:nodeRole fhir:treeRoot ;
  fhir:Resource.id [ fhir:value "normative-classification-vs"] ;
  fhir:DomainResource.text [
     fhir:Narrative.status [ fhir:value "extensions" ] ;
     fhir:Narrative.div "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><p class=\"res-header-id\"><b>Generated Narrative: ValueSet normative-classification-vs</b></p><a name=\"normative-classification-vs\"> </a><a name=\"hcnormative-classification-vs\"> </a><ul><li>Include these codes as defined in <a href=\"CodeSystem-fhir4eyes-cs.html\"><code>https://YasniiSS.github.io/fhir4eyes/CodeSystem/fhir4eyes-cs</code></a><span title=\"Version is not explicitly stated, which means it is fixed to the version provided in this specification\"> version ?0.4.0</span><table class=\"none\"><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\"><b>Code</b></td><td><b>Display</b></td><td><b>Definition</b></td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"CodeSystem-fhir4eyes-cs.html#fhir4eyes-cs-within-normal-limits\">within-normal-limits</a></td><td>Within normal limits</td><td>The measurement or analysis falls within the normal range of the device normative (age-matched reference) database (typically p &gt;= 5%).</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"CodeSystem-fhir4eyes-cs.html#fhir4eyes-cs-borderline\">borderline</a></td><td>Borderline</td><td>The measurement or analysis falls in the borderline range of the device normative database (typically 1% &lt;= p &lt; 5%).</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"CodeSystem-fhir4eyes-cs.html#fhir4eyes-cs-outside-normal-limits\">outside-normal-limits</a></td><td>Outside normal limits</td><td>The measurement or analysis falls outside the normal range of the device normative database (typically p &lt; 1%).</td></tr></table></li></ul></div>"
  ] ;
